.TH ANDROLINX 1 "September 2026" "androlinx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
androlinx \- desktop front-end for adb and scrcpy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B androlinx
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AndroLinx
puts a graphical interface on
.BR adb (1)
and
.BR scrcpy (1).
Connected phones are listed as they appear, mirroring options are kept in named
profiles, and connecting over Wi\-Fi is done from a dialog rather than by hand.
.PP
Mirroring itself is performed by scrcpy, which opens its own window. AndroLinx
finds the devices, assembles the command line and shows it before running it;
it does not embed or replace scrcpy's window.
.PP
Running AndroLinx with no options opens the window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List connected devices and exit, without opening the window.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/androlinx/config.json
Preferences, the last used device and profile, and recent wireless addresses.
.TP
.I ~/.config/androlinx/profiles.json
Profiles you have saved. The built-in profiles are not stored here.
.SH NOTES
Under Wayland a compositor does not let an application place or raise another
program's window, so scrcpy's
.B \-\-always\-on\-top
and window position options have no effect. Turning on X11 compatibility in
Preferences runs scrcpy through XWayland, where they work again.
.PP
AndroLinx never runs
.BR "adb kill-server" .
Android Studio, Waydroid and Genymotion share the same adb server, and stopping
it would disconnect them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1),
.BR scrcpy (1)
